{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed Reality.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed Reality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mixed reality mixed reality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed Reality.md","fileName":"Mixed Reality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mixed Reality","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[XR Environments]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Environments","Virtual Reality","Augmented Reality","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed Reality.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed Reality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mixed reality mixed reality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed Reality.md","fileName":"Mixed Reality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mixed Reality","heading":"Mixed Reality","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Mixed reality is a set of approaches in which real and virtual information are combined in different proportions. It includes both [[Virtual Reality]] and [[Augmented Reality]].\n\nA system can be located on a continuum whose extremes are a purely real environment and a purely virtual one. Its position on that continuum may change as the user interacts. The concept is useful because interfaces can share components and problems even when they mix physical and synthetic content differently.\n\nNear the real end, [[Augmented Reality]] makes the physical world the primary place of action and adds registered virtual information. Near the virtual end, augmented virtuality brings selected real-world imagery or participants into a primarily synthetic environment. The continuum classifies the resulting experience rather than requiring one display technology.","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Environments","Virtual Reality","Augmented Reality","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed Reality.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed Reality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mixed reality mixed reality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed Reality.md","fileName":"Mixed Reality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mixed Reality","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[augmentedreality_pearson.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Environments","Virtual Reality","Augmented Reality","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}